4. AWS has explicitly flagged the AS-LEGITAS-SET as unauthorized and the AltDB route objects as fabricated.

Your direct interconnection with AWS, if it exists, would typically be handled via AWS advertising their own prefixes in BGP sessions — not by you advertising their address space with a forged AS_PATH claiming AWS as the origin behind you.

I will continue to provide full transit for your own verified prefix (5.62.56.0/24) without interruption. If AWS wishes to route 44.192.100.0/24 through you, they should announce it themselves through their own BGP sessions with proper authorization.

Please do not re-advertise 44.192.100.0/24 to me again unless you can provide RPKI-signed authorization from AWS specifically designating AS-LEGITAS as an authorized transit provider for this prefix.
